{\rtf1\ansi\deff0{\fonttbl{\f0 \fswiss Helvetica;}{\f1 \fmodern Courier;}}
{\colortbl;\red255\green0\blue0;\red0\green0\blue255;}
\widowctrl\hyphauto

{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Converts empty items (items whose active take has no source) into real audio items by attaching a generated silent WAV. Preserves take name and item notes.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Use case: Scene Cut / Picture Cut / Subtitle tracks built with empty items can now be transferred to other DAWs together with the rest of the REAPER session, because empty items are not portable but audio items are. Mimics the EdiLoad picture-cut export style (one shared file per group).\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Behavior: \u8226 ? Scope: only operates on selected items. \u8226 ? Skips items that already have an audio source. \u8226 ? Active take only (multi-take items use the active take). \u8226 ? Items are grouped by track. Each group gets ONE shared silent WAV whose length equals the longest item in that group; all items in the group link to the same file. Per-item take name and notes are preserved. \u8226 ? Item D_LENGTH and D_POSITION are preserved (not overwritten by source).\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Output: \u8226 ? Folder: <project_path>/Media/ \u8226 ? Format: 16-bit PCM, mono, project sample rate.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Filename rules: \u8226 ? Single item, take name has no non-ASCII chars \u8594 ? use sanitized take name. \u8226 ? Otherwise (or take name is Chinese/empty) \u8594 ? "\{TrackName\}{\i \{YYMMDDHHMM\}.wav". \u8226 ? Track name also non-ASCII/empty \u8594 ? "Track\{idx\}}\{YYMMDDHHMM\}.wav". \u8226 ? Filename collisions auto-append _2, _3, ... to avoid overwriting.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Notes:\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab Based on design concepts and iterative testing by hsuanice.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab Script generated and refined with Claude.\sa180\par}
}

{\rtf1\ansi\deff0{\fonttbl{\f0 \fswiss Helvetica;}{\f1 \fmodern Courier;}}
{\colortbl;\red255\green0\blue0;\red0\green0\blue255;}
\widowctrl\hyphauto

{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel0 \b \fs36 Copy / Cut with Razor\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Copy or cut items together with envelope points, respecting razor edit areas, and move the edit cursor to the start of the selection.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel1 \b \fs32 Suggested shortcuts\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab Copy Items and Envelope Points and Move Edit Cursor to Selection Start Respect Razor: Cmd+C (or C)\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab Cut Items and Envelope Points and Move Edit Cursor to Selection Start Respect Razor: Cmd+X (or X)\sa180\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Shortcuts are suggestions only \u8212- nothing is assigned automatically. macOS names; on Windows Cmd = Ctrl, Option = Alt, Control = Win.\par}
}

{\rtf1\ansi\deff0{\fonttbl{\f0 \fswiss Helvetica;}{\f1 \fmodern Courier;}}
{\colortbl;\red255\green0\blue0;\red0\green0\blue255;}
\widowctrl\hyphauto

{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Non-destructive helper for vocal comping. This script never moves or edits child items.\par}
}

{\rtf1\ansi\deff0{\fonttbl{\f0 \fswiss Helvetica;}{\f1 \fmodern Courier;}}
{\colortbl;\red255\green0\blue0;\red0\green0\blue255;}
\widowctrl\hyphauto

{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Workflow script for poly WAV production:\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 1)\tx360\tab Explode selected multichannel items to new one-channel items on new tracks (non-destructive).\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 2)\tx360\tab Render each exploded mono item to a new take with command 40601.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 3)\tx360\tab Re-embed metadata from Take 1 to the rendered active take using hsuanice_Metadata Embed.lua.\sa180\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Notes:\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab Explode step preserves the original source in Take 1.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab Render step creates a new mono file in the active take.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab Metadata embed is strict 1:1: mono output N receives source metadata slot N, including empty slots.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab Track/take naming currently follows Rodilab-style numeric suffixes for easy later adjustment.\sa180\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Requirements:\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab BWF MetaEdit CLI available to the Metadata Embed library.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab hsuanice_Metadata Embed.lua in the hsuanice Scripts/Library folder.\sa180\par}
}

{\rtf1\ansi\deff0{\fonttbl{\f0 \fswiss Helvetica;}{\f1 \fmodern Courier;}}
{\colortbl;\red255\green0\blue0;\red0\green0\blue255;}
\widowctrl\hyphauto

{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Runs REAPER's built-in "Take: Explode takes of items across tracks" (action 40224) and then renames all resulting tracks based on the source track name.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Items with only 1 take are copied to all new tracks (action 40224 normally leaves them only on the source track).\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Example: source track "EDL - A1" with items that have 3 takes \u8594 ? results in: EDL - A1 (source track, untouched) EDL - A1 - 1 EDL - A1 - 2 EDL - A1 - 3\par}
}

{\rtf1\ansi\deff0{\fonttbl{\f0 \fswiss Helvetica;}{\f1 \fmodern Courier;}}
{\colortbl;\red255\green0\blue0;\red0\green0\blue255;}
\widowctrl\hyphauto

{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel0 \b \fs36 Fix Tools\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Find and fix edit details that other DAWs handle differently when a REAPER session is exported.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab Fix Edges Off Grid\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab Fix Looped Source Items\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab Fix Misaligned Crossfades\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab Fix Overlap Items (partial or complete)\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab Fix Split Items at Fade Edges\sa180\par}
}

{\rtf1\ansi\deff0{\fonttbl{\f0 \fswiss Helvetica;}{\f1 \fmodern Courier;}}
{\colortbl;\red255\green0\blue0;\red0\green0\blue255;}
\widowctrl\hyphauto

{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel0 \b \fs36 Hover Mode\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Pro Tools-style editing that follows the mouse (Hover Mode on) or the edit cursor (Hover Mode off).\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab Toggle: switch Hover Mode on/off (toolbar-friendly)\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab Split: split items at the selection, edit cursor or mouse\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab Trim Left / Right: trim or extend the item edge to the cursor, keeping fades\sa180\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Hover Mode Toggle is based on / inspired by TJF's "Hover Mode Toggle" script.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel1 \b \fs32 Suggested shortcuts\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab Hover Mode Split Item by Selection or Edit or Mouse Cursor: B\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab Hover Mode Trim or Extend Left Edge of Item: A\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab Hover Mode Trim or Extend Right Edge of Item: S\sa180\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Shortcuts are suggestions only \u8212- nothing is assigned automatically. macOS names; on Windows Cmd = Ctrl, Option = Alt, Control = Win.\par}
}

{\rtf1\ansi\deff0{\fonttbl{\f0 \fswiss Helvetica;}{\f1 \fmodern Courier;}}
