{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 A GUI tool for repositioning selected items with flexible options.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab Supports interval units: Seconds / Frames / Grid.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab Choose position from Item Start or End.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab Cross-track or per-track modes supported.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab Includes Undo / Redo buttons for keyboard-less workflows.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab Real-time adjustable via ImGUI with auto-resize.\sa180\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \u55357 ?\u56481 ? Designed for precise spacing and layout control in complex editing sessions. Integrates with hsuanice\u8217's ReaImGui workflow tools for item/selection editing.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 This script was generated using ChatGPT based on design concepts and iterative testing by hsuanice. hsuanice served as the workflow designer, tester, and integrator for this tool.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Features:\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab Built with ReaImGUI for a compact, responsive UI.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab Designed for fast, keyboard-light workflows.\sa180\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 References:\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab REAPER ReaScript API (Lua)\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab ReaImGUI (ReaScript ImGui binding)\sa180\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Note:\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab This is a 0.1 beta release for internal testing.\sa180\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 This script was generated using ChatGPT based on design concepts and iterative testing by hsuanice. hsuanice served as the workflow designer, tester, and integrator for this tool.\par}
}

{\rtf1\ansi\deff0{\fonttbl{\f0 \fswiss Helvetica;}{\f1 \fmodern Courier;}}
{\colortbl;\red255\green0\blue0;\red0\green0\blue255;}
\widowctrl\hyphauto

{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Moves the currently selected items (one or many, possibly spanning multiple tracks) to the track that the mouse cursor is hovering over. Timeline position is preserved \u8212- only the vertical (track) position changes.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Acts as a one-step "vertical cut & paste":\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab No need to cut, scroll, click target track, then paste.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab Just select items, hover over the target track, run the action.\sa180\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Behavior: \u8226 ? Scope: operates on the current item selection. \u8226 ? The topmost selected track is aligned to the track under the mouse. All other selected items keep their relative track offsets, so multi- track selections move together as a block. \u8226 ? If the destination span exceeds the last track, new empty tracks are auto-appended at the bottom of the project so all items have a home. \u8226 ? If any moved item would overlap an existing item on its destination track, a warning dialog is shown with three options: Yes (Insert) \u8212- Insert N empty tracks at the destination so the selection lands on fresh, empty tracks. No (Overwrite) \u8212- Trim/split existing items in the overlap range, then place the moved items on top. Cancel \u8212- Abort. \u8226 ? If the mouse is not over any track (e.g. over TCP empty area, ruler, or master), the script does nothing. \u8226 ? If the target offset is zero (mouse already on the topmost selected track), the script does nothing.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Notes:\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab Designed for keyboard/mouse-modifier workflow (assign to a shortcut and trigger while hovering the destination track).\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab Based on design concepts and iterative testing by hsuanice.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab Script generated and refined with Claude.\sa180\par}
}

{\rtf1\ansi\deff0{\fonttbl{\f0 \fswiss Helvetica;}{\f1 \fmodern Courier;}}
{\colortbl;\red255\green0\blue0;\red0\green0\blue255;}
\widowctrl\hyphauto

{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Provides three vertical re-arrangement modes for selected items (stacked UI):\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \u8226 ? Reorder (fill upward)\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab Keeps items at their original timeline position.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab Packs items upward into available selected tracks, avoiding gaps.\sa180\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \u8226 ? Sort Vertically\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab Groups items by near-identical start time.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab Within each time cluster, re-orders items top-to-bottom by: Take Name / File Name / Metadata (Track Name or Channel Number).\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab Ascending / Descending toggle.\sa180\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \u8226 ? Metadata modes\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab Copy to Sort: duplicates selected items to NEW tracks grouped by metadata.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab Sort in Place: reorders items on their existing tracks based on metadata (Track Name or Channel Number). No new tracks are created, no names changed.\sa180\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Notes:\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab Based on design concepts and iterative testing by hsuanice.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab Script generated and refined with ChatGPT.\sa180\par}
}

{\rtf1\ansi\deff0{\fonttbl{\f0 \fswiss Helvetica;}{\f1 \fmodern Courier;}}
{\colortbl;\red255\green0\blue0;\red0\green0\blue255;}
\widowctrl\hyphauto

{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel1 \b \fs32 Suggested shortcuts\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab Toggle Mute Item under Mouse Cursor: Control+M\sa180\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Shortcuts are suggestions only \u8212- nothing is assigned automatically. macOS names; on Windows Cmd = Ctrl, Option = Alt, Control = Win.\par}
}

{\rtf1\ansi\deff0{\fonttbl{\f0 \fswiss Helvetica;}{\f1 \fmodern Courier;}}
{\colortbl;\red255\green0\blue0;\red0\green0\blue255;}
\widowctrl\hyphauto

{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Config-driven color palette with keyword rules \u8212- colors items by take name.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Palette is generated from Hue + per-row Saturation/Value settings (like rodilab's Color palette). Shiny mode follows the ShinyColor behavior of Chroma - Coloring Tool by OLSHALOM (https://forum.cockos.com/showthread.php?t=281516). Right-click any swatch \u8594 ? Edit Color / Edit Keyword / Clear Keyword Left-click a swatch \u8594 ? apply that color to selected items Auto Color mode colors all items automatically on project changes\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 No external dependencies \u8212- REAPER built-in GFX library.\par}
}

{\rtf1\ansi\deff0{\fonttbl{\f0 \fswiss Helvetica;}{\f1 \fmodern Courier;}}
{\colortbl;\red255\green0\blue0;\red0\green0\blue255;}
\widowctrl\hyphauto

{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel0 \b \fs36 hsuanice Library\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Shared code used by hsuanice scripts (RGWH, AudioSweet, Hover Mode, Reorder, ...). Install this package together with any hsuanice script. It adds nothing to the Action List.\par}
}

{\rtf1\ansi\deff0{\fonttbl{\f0 \fswiss Helvetica;}{\f1 \fmodern Courier;}}
{\colortbl;\red255\green0\blue0;\red0\green0\blue255;}
\widowctrl\hyphauto

{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel0 \b \fs36 AudioSweet ReaImGui\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Complete AudioSweet control center with ImGui interface for managing FX chains and presets.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel1 \b \fs32 Quick Start\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab Help \u8594 ? User Manual: Full documentation with workflows and tips\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab Help \u8594 ? About: Reference and credits\sa180\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel1 \b \fs32 Reference\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Inspired by AudioSuite-like Script by Tim Chimes 'AudioSweet' is a name originally given by Tim Chimes. This project continues to use the name in reference to his original work.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Original: Renders selected plugin to selected media item Written for REAPER 5.1 with Lua v1.1 12/22/2015 - Added PreventUIRefresh http://timchimes.com/scripting-with-reaper-audiosuite/\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel1 \b \fs32 Development\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 This script was developed with the assistance of AI tools including ChatGPT and Claude AI.\par}
}

{\rtf1\ansi\deff0{\fonttbl{\f0 \fswiss Helvetica;}{\f1 \fmodern Courier;}}
{\colortbl;\red255\green0\blue0;\red0\green0\blue255;}
\widowctrl\hyphauto

{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 ImGui-based GUI for configuring and running RGWH Core operations. Provides visual controls for all RGWH Wrapper Template parameters.\par}
}

{\rtf1\ansi\deff0{\fonttbl{\f0 \fswiss Helvetica;}{\f1 \fmodern Courier;}}
{\colortbl;\red255\green0\blue0;\red0\green0\blue255;}
\widowctrl\hyphauto

{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Single-button toggle watcher that add-selects media items on each track according to that track's TRACK-LEVEL Razor Areas (GUID == ""). Envelope-lane razors are preserved but ignored for matching.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 MODE (user option inside the script): \u8226 ? RANGE_MODE = 1 \u8594 ? Overlap : item is selected if it INTERSECTS any Razor range \u8226 ? RANGE_MODE = 2 \u8594 ? Contain : item is selected only if it is FULLY inside a Razor range (INCLUSIVE with tiny EPS tolerance, so equal-length is selected; Pro Tools-like)\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Behavior: \u8226 ? Add-only selection (does not clear existing item selection unless STRICT_SYNC = true). \u8226 ? Does not modify Razor Areas; only reads them. \u8226 ? Relaunching terminates the previous instance and keeps a toolbar toggle in sync.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Note: This script was generated using ChatGPT based on design concepts and iterative testing by hsuanice. hsuanice served as the workflow designer, tester, and integrator for this tool.\par}
}

{\rtf1\ansi\deff0{\fonttbl{\f0 \fswiss Helvetica;}{\f1 \fmodern Courier;}}
{\colortbl;\red255\green0\blue0;\red0\green0\blue255;}
\widowctrl\hyphauto

{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Toggle (background watcher). After a right-button DRAG, on the frame the button is released (optionally one frame later) the time selection is set to the earliest start / latest end of the currently selected items. Optimized for large projects: a single pass over the selected items on release (no GUID table, no before/after diff), and an optional skip when the time selection would not change. Requires hsuanice_Mouse.lua (hsuanice Library) and the js_ReaScriptAPI extension.\par}
}

{\rtf1\ansi\deff0{\fonttbl{\f0 \fswiss Helvetica;}{\f1 \fmodern Courier;}}
{\colortbl;\red255\green0\blue0;\red0\green0\blue255;}
\widowctrl\hyphauto

{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Pro Tools-style "Link Track and Edit Selection". Edit Selection = Razor Area or Item Selection.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Perf principles: \u8226 ? Gate heavy scans by GetProjectStateChangeCount(). \u8226 ? Enumerate ONLY selected tracks/items when possible. \u8226 ? Cache per-track Razor; recompute on project-state changes only. \u8226 ? Apply changes only on delta tracks; publish ExtState only on change. \u8226 ? Keep Latched Virtual Range; avoid shrinking on track toggles.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Priority:\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 1)\tx360\tab Razor exists \u8594 ? use Razor (highest)\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 2)\tx360\tab Else Item Selection \u8594 ? use VIRTUAL (latched) span [min..max]\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 3)\tx360\tab Else no active range\sa180\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Notes: \u8226 ? ABCD switches added (USER OPTIONS) to enable/disable each main section: A) Razor changed \u8594 ? Track selection follows "tracks with Razor" B) Items changed (no Razor) \u8594 ? Track selection follows items' tracks C) Track selection changed + REAL TS \u8594 ? build/clear Razor + sync items (Overlap) D) Razor/Track changed \u8594 ? sync items under ACTIVE range on changed tracks \u8226 ? DEBUG_PRINT will log which section fired (A/B/C/D) for instant diagnosis.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Credits: This script was generated using ChatGPT based on design concepts and iterative testing by hsuanice. hsuanice served as the workflow designer, tester, and integrator for this tool.\par}
}

{\rtf1\ansi\deff0{\fonttbl{\f0 \fswiss Helvetica;}{\f1 \fmodern Courier;}}
{\colortbl;\red255\green0\blue0;\red0\green0\blue255;}
\widowctrl\hyphauto

{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 After an AAF import, split-stereo tracks (e.g. "Audio 9_L" / "Audio 9_R") arrive panned center. This script scans ALL tracks and pans each adjacent L/R pair: \u8226 ? L track -> 100% Left, R track -> 100% Right \u8226 ? A pair = track N ends with an L suffix AND track N+1 has the same base name with an R suffix \u8226 ? Recognized suffixes (case-insensitive): _L/_R, -L/-R, .L/.R, " L"/" R" Unpaired L/R-looking tracks are left untouched and listed in a message for review. Notes:\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab Works with every pan mode; in Dual Pan mode both knobs are set to the same side.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab Single undo point.\sa180\par}
}

{\rtf1\ansi\deff0{\fonttbl{\f0 \fswiss Helvetica;}{\f1 \fmodern Courier;}}
{\colortbl;\red255\green0\blue0;\red0\green0\blue255;}
\widowctrl\hyphauto

{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Delete selected tracks with safety: \u8226 ? If ALL selected tracks are empty (no items, no automation/envelope data, no FX inserts, no input FX, no sends/receives) AND none is a folder parent with children, delete immediately with no prompt. \u8226 ? Otherwise (any content, folder parents with children, or FX/routing present), show a detailed summary and ask for confirmation. \u8226 ? Summary includes: selected track count, items, automation tracks, folder parents, total child tracks, FX inserts, input FX, sends, receives. Notes:\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab "Automation present" = any track envelope has \u8805 ?1 point OR \u8805 ?1 automation item.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab "Folder parent with children" = a selected track whose next track depth is greater than its own.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab Child tracks counting includes all descendants under each selected folder parent (until depth returns to or above the parent's depth).\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab Master track is ignored by REAPER's CountSelectedTracks().\sa180\par}
}

{\rtf1\ansi\deff0{\fonttbl{\f0 \fswiss Helvetica;}{\f1 \fmodern Courier;}}
